{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>תשיך</b> — Twice in the Masorah: כל דבר אשר ישך, כנחש ישך. For interest is like one bitten by a snake, which rises little by little and he does not feel it until it swells to a great sum, like the bite of a snake. 'Neder' is juxtaposed to 'לא תשיך' — lest you say: I will take interest in order to pay my vows."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:28.542285577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}